title The meter that counts one call -- Amphora's eight take all three builds, and a repair sized to the reading is undersized
prompt Keaton seated the Silence loop: read Kyri and Gauge, honor the ITINERARY inner loop, pick up the running thread, work the infrastructure lane, stop at custody gates.
think ListAgents named one peer, grain-a7, and I sent it my twelve intended paths before a file moved -- the whole of what REDS %291 leaves an agent able to do while one-tree-per-star stays Keaton's word. The peer answered by working: four LOCA commits landed during my cold roster and a fifth, 22bd44144, landed while I patched, so HEAD moved under me twice inside one lap and my working tree survived only because our path sets never crossed.
think Reds first. Nine rows read OPEN in the pin and eight are held elsewhere -- %291 and %327 Keaton's hand, %311 Sound's language custody, %326 and %328 seats, %330 its own design lap, %301 five booked folds, %306 a seat. One was agent-closable and in this lane: %334, where a witness names its build in a comment and then runs a gitignored binary. Amphora was the largest remaining block, 17 of the 38 pairs across 8 of the 28 witnesses, so it was both the crux and the continuation of last lap's Mandate seven.
think I sized the repair from the scan's own --list output: three artifacts, seventeen pairs, a per-file list of exactly what each witness names in run position. That list was wrong, and it was wrong in the direction a meter is always wrong -- it reads one edge.
obs The catch came from how the proof was run rather than from reading anything. The first sweep ran all eight back to back and printed eight greens; pour built all three binaries and the seven behind it read green off pour's leavings. That is the borrowed-state green %334 exists to book, reproduced inside its own repair, and I had it in hand for about a minute before wiping amphora/bin/ ahead of each run turned four of the eight into honest reds -- pour_negative, carry_negative, restore, restore_negative, every one dying at its first pour.
obs The root is in the module rather than the meter: amphora/src/main.rye:138 and :176 resolve vessel-seal and vessel-core as sibling subprocesses, so a witness naming only amphora in run position still needs all three on disk. The scan's own THE HONEST LIMIT paragraph says the reading is narrow; what was missing is the consequence, which is that satisfying it exactly can leave the defect standing.
obs The sharper half was a credited pair. rye build refuses an absent -femit-bin directory -- measured, "unable to open output directory 'amphora/bin': FileNotFound" -- and the build line already standing in amphora_first_resident_witness.rish carried no mkdir. The scan counted it self_built while it could not have run on a clone, which is a claim proven only in the passing direction wearing a build line.
obs Booked as REDS %337, born on its shelf as %335 and %336 were, since the pin stands at 24,571 of 24,576 and every elder row still reads OPEN. Next free read 337 from the anointed spine after a fetch, per fetch-before-book.
obs The cold roster closed guard_red with tree_moved=yes -- the fourth consecutive lap for this seat. Seven guards red, and I could name only six from my own capture: I piped the run through tail -60, which threw away the head, and recovered the seventh from construction/standing-equipment-reds/ instead. That is a self-inflicted blind spot and the fix is one word -- tee, never tail.
obs The seventh is the one worth another hand: dated_path reads refs_lost=335 against lost_ceiling=168, with broken_gone=296 of 19,861 broken references over 25,479 homes. It was red before I touched a file, so it is not this lap's, and it is not small. The cheap first move is a --list mode on tools/fixtures/d/dated_path_scan.sh, which has none: the census can count the gone set and cannot name it, so nobody can start.
obs remember_git_nib read red on a card nib naming 7c7cf08623, a hash in no object store here -- the %315 shape one day after %315 closed, arriving from another body whose pre-amend hash never reached the spine. Repaired the way %315 seated it: this round's card names HEAD's parent, a commit the remote already carries, so no amend races the peer.
